      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a decent start but it feels a bit light. i think we need to make the tone even more cooperative so they don't just get defensive and shut down. \n\ncan you try a second version? try to lean more into the \"conciliatory\" side of things. basically, make it sound like we are really looking to find common ground and be reasonable, while still keeping that boundary about the exclusivity clause. i don't want it to look like we're being difficult, but we definitely can't concede on the arbitration point. \n\njust make sure it actually reads like a legal professional wrote it and doesn't just look like a list of concessions.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
